  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I was working with a local web files directory (Path To Web Content), and wanted to try using jQuery.\n\nBecause VRC_WebPanel only lets you choose a directory from the project assets, jQuery's .js file has to be in your project assets.\n\nUnity will then look at all .js files in the project assets, and run its own completely different validation on them (because it's a supported language for writing Unity scripts!), deciding in many cases that the file is corrupt. This is the case for both jQuery and three.js, and most likely any other non-trivial, real javascript library someone might want to use.\n\nThe end result is that when you try to test or upload your world, the new version will not be uploaded if such js files are present.\n\nProposed solution: Allow specifying a file path _outside_ the assets directory so that these files don't get picked up by Unity at all.\n\nKnown workaround: Host the files up on a web server instead.",
